# ONE universal ignore file, shared by all three Cloud Run images (Dockerfile,
# Dockerfile.frontend, Dockerfile.admin). This intentionally does NOT try to scope down to any
# single image's own needs — that was the previous design (a `Dockerfile.frontend.dockerignore`/
# `Dockerfile.admin.dockerignore` pair meant to override this file per Docker BuildKit's
# `<dockerfile-name>.dockerignore` convention) and it silently broke every image except the
# default `Dockerfile`: Google Cloud Build's own build step (Kaniko, and `gcloud run deploy
# --source`'s default builder) does NOT implement that BuildKit-only naming convention — it reads
# only the file literally named `.dockerignore` at the build context root, no matter which
# `--dockerfile`/`-f` was given. Concretely, that meant every `gcloud run deploy --source .
# --dockerfile Dockerfile.frontend` build actually ran against THIS file — which excluded
# `tsconfig.json`, `src/`, etc. for the (unrelated) backend's sake — producing exactly the
# `TS5083: Cannot read file '/app/tsconfig.json'` failure this file's rewrite fixes.
#
# The correct, portable fix (works identically under Cloud Build, Kaniko, plain `docker build`,
# and BuildKit): this file only ever excludes things NONE of the three images' own explicit
# `COPY <name> <name>` instructions ever reference — never `src`, `backend`, `shared`,
# `tsconfig*.json`, `vite*.config.ts`, or any of the route directories. Each Dockerfile's build
# stage names exactly what it needs; nothing relies on this file to narrow scope further. A file
# that's present here but genuinely irrelevant to a given image (e.g. `backend/` inside
# Dockerfile.frontend's build stage, needed only because `src/admin/*.ts` type-imports from it)
# is harmless — multi-stage builds discard the build stage entirely; only the final stage's own
# explicit `COPY --from=build ...` ships anything into the deployed image.
node_modules
dist
dist-admin
dist-server

.git
.github

# Content pipeline + one-off scripts — CLI-only, never imported by app or build code.
pipeline
data
scripts

tests
e2e
docs
*.md

.env
.env.*
*.local
.DS_Store
*.tsbuildinfo
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
